        "html": "<style>.opt{border:1px solid #d7dedb;border-radius:10px;padding:10px 12px;margin-bottom:10px}.opt h4{margin:0 0 6px;font-size:15px}.opt p{margin:2px 0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35}.tag{display:inline-block;font-size:11px;padding:1px 8px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2f0;margin-left:6px}.best{border-color:#a6d94f}.fast{border-color:#00a2e1}.risk{border-color:#ff7fa3}</style><div class=\"opt fast\"><h4>1 · Full rollback <span class=\"tag\">fastest escape hatch</span></h4><p>Pro: recovers service fastest.</p><p>Con: removes two unrelated checkout improvements.</p></div><div class=\"opt risk\"><h4>2 · Larger connection pool <span class=\"tag\">treats symptom</span></h4><p>Pro: eases immediate pressure.</p><p>Con: only temporary relief; can push more load into the database.</p></div><div class=\"opt best\"><h4>3 · Narrow retry rollback + concurrency cap <span class=\"tag\">best balance</span></h4><p>Pro: targets the suspected retry feedback loop directly.</p><p>Con: needs strict conditions to hold.</p></div>"
